' Where the effective filter comes from (RFC 0009, "URL and persistence").
@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #1e1e1e
skinparam ArrowColor #1e1e1e

start
if (URL carries a service set in svcFilter?) then (yes)
  #fff3bf:Service hide set
  from svcFilter (a stale one hides nothing);
else (no)
  :Saved service default
  (localStorage, written only by Save as Default),
  unless it would leave no span, and not again
  for the same URL after an edit or a URL cleanup;
endif
if (URL carries svcFilter, f or tree?) then (yes)
  #fff3bf:Other clauses and tree mode
  from f=… and tree=lift;
else (no)
  :View default
  (Timeline: none. GenAI view of a GenAI trace:
  hide Non-GenAI, lift children, unless that
  would leave no span with the services hidden);
endif
:uiFind text, from the URL in either case;
:Effective clauses
→ findIDs, hiddenIDs;
note right
  Clearing the filter in the GenAI view writes
  an explicitly empty clause list to the URL, which
  later edits keep, so the view default does not return.
end note
stop
@enduml
